{"id": "wwdc2017-718", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/718", "wordCount": 1394, "segments": [{"start": 17.0, "text": "Welcome."}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "This year, we are delighted to"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "introduce a new framework in iOS"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "11 called Core NFC, that would"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "allow your apps to integrate NFC"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "on iPhone 7 and iPhone 7 Plus."}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "Using Core NFC, apps can"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "interact with their physical"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "environment and the real-world"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "objects within it."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "You may already know that Apple"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "Pay uses NFC for complex"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "payment."}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "Now, with the introduction of"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "Core NFC, you will be able to"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "use NFC in your applications to"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "create new and innovative user"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "experiences with the iPhone."}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "In this session, we will give"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "you a brief overview of new"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "field communications, what is"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "supported in the Core NFC"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "framework, the requirements and"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "details for using it, and some"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "example code."}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "To start off, let's talk a"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "little bit about Near Field"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "Communication."}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "Near Field Communication, known"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "simply as NFC, is a wireless"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "technology that allows the"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "exchange of information between"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "devices that are within close"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "proximity."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "Limited to a range of just a few"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "centimeters."}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "NFC is actually a collection of"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "a number of different standards"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "and protocols."}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "All of these standards coexist"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "and are used in different"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "You may have seen or had"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "experience with NFC text."}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "The small little stickers or"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "cards which can be read"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "wirelessly by an NFC reader."}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "NFC text comes in a wide variety"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "of shapes, sizes, and"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "capacities."}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "They are classified into five"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "categories, known as Type 1"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "through Type 5."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "Each one corresponding to a"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "different standard."}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "For example, Type 3 texts are"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "based on FEDECA [assumed"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "spelling] and Type 4 is based on"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "ISO-14443."}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "The NFC Forum has defined the"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "NFC Data Exchange Format, or"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "NDEF for short, as a common"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "messaging format for exchanging"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "data in a standardized way among"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "the different text types."}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "Now that we have covered some"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "NFC basics, let's take a look at"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "what you can do with Core NFC."}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "For the initial launch of Core"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "NFC, we have focused on NFC Tag"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "Reading, which can be used to"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "enhance the user experience in a"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "wide variety of ways."}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "Potential applications include"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "connecting user to location or"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "context-specific content,"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "connecting physical hardware"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "with your application, and even"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "for in-store product information"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "or inventory tracking."}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "In addition, NFC Tags can be"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "used in place of QR codes."}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "Core NFC will allow your"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "application to read any NDEF"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "formatted tag."}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "This greatly simplifies the"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "process of reading tags within"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "your application or for having"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "to deal with the different"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "standards."}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "Tag reading is supported on"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "iPhone 7 and iPhone 7 Plus."}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "At this time, Core NFC does not"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "support writing or formatting"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "operations."}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "There are two requirements for"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "using Core NFC in your"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "First, Core NFC is an"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "entitlement-protective"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "You will need to turn on the"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "Near Field Communication Tag"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "Reading Capability from Xcode to"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "get this entitlement."}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "However, this capability would"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "not be in Xcode for the first"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "released at WWDC."}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "In the meantime, you can"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "manually request this"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "entitlement by visiting the"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "Certificates, Identifiers and"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "Profiles page on the Apple"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "Developer website."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "The second requirement for Core"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "NFC is a Scan Usage Description."}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "This string is required in your"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "application's info P-list file,"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "and it will be displayed to the"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "user when your application"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "starts NFC scanning."}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "For more information, you can"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "watch the WWDC session, Privacy"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "and Your Apps."}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "Now that you have configured"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "your project correctly, let's"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "review some additional details"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "about tag reading with the Core"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "NFC framework."}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "First, tag reading is an"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "on-demand process, meaning that"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "your application has to initiate"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "a tag reading activity using a"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "Second, your application has to"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "be visible and foregrounded in"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "order to start a tag reading"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "activity."}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "A tag reading session will be"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "ended if your application is"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "backgrounded or ceases to be"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "visible."}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "Next, each tag reading activity"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "is limited to 60 seconds at a"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "time. If a session has timed out or"}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "invalidated, your application"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "must create a new session to"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "initiate another tag reading"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "activity."}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "You can configure a session to"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "read either a single tag or"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "multiple tags."}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "In a single tag reading mode,"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "the session will be ended"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "automatically after a tag is"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "read."}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "On the other hand, a multi-tag"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "reading session will remain"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "active until canceled by the"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "user, or the 60-second timeout"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "is reached."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "Finally, as mentioned"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "previously, the NFC Usage String"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "defined in your info P-list will"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "be displayed to the user while"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "the tag reading activity is in"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "progress."}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "We have provided a sample"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "application along with this"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "presentation to demonstrate the"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "use of Core NFC."}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "Consider the case where you want"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "to take a physical kind of"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "inventory."}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "Here, we are showing you the key"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "user interaction sequence of the"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "sample application."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "The sample application consists"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "of a main table view, and a Scan"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "button."}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "Every time an inventory item is"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "scanned, it is displayed as a"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "role entry in this main table"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "view."}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "Just click on the Scan button to"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "start a tag scanning."}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "This UI will be presented to the"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "user hopefully on top of your"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "application once tag scanning"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "has begun."}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "During tag scanning, the user's"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "description string is displayed"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "within the UI."}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "At any time, the user can hit"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "the Cancel button to stop a tag"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "scanning, which will invalidate"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "the reader session."}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "The UI will get updated once an"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "NFC tag has been successfully"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "read."}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "Here, we have configured our"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "reader session to be single tag"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "read mode."}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "Finally, the overlaid UI will be"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "dismissed, and the application"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "will be foregrounded once the"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "tag reading session has ended."}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "All right."}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "Let's walk through the code"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "together from the sample"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "application we have just shown."}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "At a high level, you would need"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "to perform these three easy"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "steps to enable tag reading in"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "your application."}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "First, adopt the NFC NDEF Reader"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "Session Delegate Protocol."}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "Next, create an instance of the"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "NFC NDEF Reader Session Class,"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "and provide it with your"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "delegate."}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "Finally, start a reader session"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "using the Begin method, and"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "handle the delegate callbacks."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "Here is a cool snippet from the"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "sample application, illustrating"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "the three-step approach."}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "To start off, we import the Core"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "NFC framework into the code."}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "Here we adopt the delegate"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "protocol in Table View"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "Controller, which will handle"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "the two required callbacks."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "They invalidate with error and"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "detect NDEF."}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "The invalidate with error"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "callback will notify your"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "application when a tag reading"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "activity has stopped."}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "This can happen for a variety of"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "reasons."}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "For example, a tag has been"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "successfully read in a single"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "tag read session."}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "The user has chosen to stop the"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "tag scanning activity."}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "The 3-second timeout has expired"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "or the application is no longer"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "in the foreground."}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "The specific session object"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "provided in the first parameter"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "will be invalidated after the"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "function exits."}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "A new reader session instance is"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "required for additional tag"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "reading."}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "The detect NDEFs will be invoked"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "every time an NDEF has been read"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "from an NFC tag."}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "Your application can then grab"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "the payload from the NDEF"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "message, decode it, and handle"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "the message as appropriate."}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "Finally, we have an extra method"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "that links to the Scan button"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "for starting a single tag read"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "All you need to do is create an"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "instance of NFC NDEF Reader"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "Session with your data gate,"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "then invoke to begin method to"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "start tag scanning."}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "If you wish to create a"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "multi-tag reading session, set"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "the invalidate at the first read"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "parameter to False."}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "If you need to stop an ongoing"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "session programmatically, you"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "can call the invalidate method."}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "This will trigger your"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "invalidate with error callback,"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "letting you know that the"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "session has ended."}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "In summary, it is very simple to"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "enable NFC tag reading with Core"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "NFC by following these steps."}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "Enable the NFC tag reading"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "capability."}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "Make sure your Scan Usage"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "Description String is set in"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "your info P-list."}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "Integrate the Core NFC framework"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "in your code."}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "And start reading tags."}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "For more information about this"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "presentation and our sample"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "code, please visit this online"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "link."}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "Also, here are some related"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "sessions you might be interested"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "in."}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "Privacy and Your Apps will"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "discuss important"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "privacy-related topics, and"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "What's New In Apple Pay and"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "Wallet will talk about all the"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "exciting Apple Pay features"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "coming to iOS and Mac OS."}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "Thank you for watching this"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "presentation on Core NFC"}]}